## class
A class defines the attributes (data) and methods (functions) that the objects
created from the class will have.

## object 
An object is an instance of a class.

## variable
A variable is a named reference to a value or object stored in memory.
It acts as a container that holds data, which can be accessed, modified,
or used in computations throughout a program.

## attribute
Attributes are the properties or characteristics of an object and
are accessed using dot notation (e.g., object.attribute)

## function
Functions help organize code, promote reusability, and make programs easier
to understand and maintain. They are defined using the def keyword and can be
called by their name with appropriate arguments.

## method 
A method is a function that is defined inside a class and is associated
with an object (instance) or the class itself.
    like:- def keyword, self , cls, __init__, __str__
    